emitted `trust_basis` value for each path (`own_key`, `pinned_environment`, `envelope_key`), not just the accept/reject verdict.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Surface the chosen basis as a new `trust_basis` result field.'","Schema impact: 'document `trust_basis`'","AC1-AC5 assert verdicts (foreign_key/mismatch/accept) but none assert the trust_basis label value"],"finding":"The new `trust_basis` result field (Design item 3, added to verify_signature_result.schema.json) has no acceptance criterion that asserts its emitted VALUE. AC2 exercises the pinned-key requirement but does not assert `trust_basis: \"pinned_environment\"`; no AC asserts `own_key` or `envelope_key` labeling. A described deliverable is left without a covering criterion.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f34da16f18cd6336a","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design item 3 / File impact (schema) / Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"ne4af749d0756110b","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A regression labels an envelope-key acceptance as `own_key` and no AC catches it","trust_basis is added to the schema but never populated correctly and tests still pass"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Extend AC1/AC2 (or add AC6) to assert `trust_basis == \"envelope_key\"` on the advisory cross-env accept and `trust_basis == \"pinned_environment\"` under enforcement.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add `src/rebar/_mcp_models.py` (VerifySignatureResultOut) and `src/rebar/types.py` (VerifySignatureResult TypedDict) to File impact and update both to carry `trust_basis`, so the check_mcp_models schema-drift validator and the typed mirrors stay in sync with the narrowed-verdict schema.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0444,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["check_mcp_models.py MODEL_SCHEMAS maps 'VerifySignatureResultOut': 'verify_signature_result'; module docstring: 'checks for missing declarations — schema properties that no model field covers — and fails the build when any are found'","src/rebar/_mcp_models.py:359 `class VerifySignatureResultOut(_Out)` enumerates the fields explicitly (no trust_basis)","src/rebar/types.py:302 `class VerifySignatureResult(TypedDict)` mirrors the verdict Literal enum and field set","tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_model_schema_drift_heldout.py:57 imports VerifySignatureResultOut and asserts requiredness matches the schema"],"finding":"The plan changes verify_signature_result.schema.json (adds `trust_basis`, narrows `foreign_key`) but omits from File impact the two hand-maintained code mirrors of that schema that live outside the edited files: `VerifySignatureResultOut` in src/rebar/_mcp_models.py and `VerifySignatureResult` in src/rebar/types.py. src/rebar/schemas/check_mcp_models.py runs a drift validator (invoked by tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_model_schema_drift_heldout.py) that FAILS the build when a schema property has no covering model field — so adding `trust_basis` to the schema without declaring it on VerifySignatureResultOut will break `make test`/`make lint`.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f963652e65f835691","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"File impact — `src/rebar/schemas/verify_signature_result.schema.json` line; and Testing (`make lint`, `make test`)","norm_id":"n19024e6f5b8d81e6","priority":0.7556,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Schema gains `trust_basis` property; check_mcp_models --check reports a missing declaration on VerifySignatureResultOut and exits 1","A downstream typed consumer reads result['trust_basis'] but the TypedDict/pydantic mirror never declared it"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In File impact, add the two schema mirrors and declare `trust_basis: str | None = None` on VerifySignatureResultOut plus the corresponding NotRequired field on the VerifySignatureResult TypedDict; keep the verdict enum consistent across schema, TypedDict, and any narrowed foreign_key description.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["3 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable).","vague/subjective terms present: good"],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the exact activation predicate combining `verify.require_environment` and `opcert_enforce_since` (both-required vs since-guard) so the executor need not infer it.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.5525,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Design item 1: '`_required_environment(repo_root)` — reads `verify.require_environment`'","AC2: 'With `verify.require_environment` + `opcert_enforce_since` both set'","AC1: 'With `verify.require_environment`/`opcert_enforce_since` unset'"],"finding":"The relationship between the two enforcement keys `verify.require_environment` and `opcert_enforce_since` is under-specified. Design item 1 says `_required_environment` reads only `verify.require_environment`, while AC1 gates advisory mode on BOTH being unset and AC2 gates enforcement on BOTH being set. Whether enforcement requires both keys, either key, or one is a since-guard for the other is not stated.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f032d792d992d7727","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design item 1 / AC1 / AC2","norm_id":"n17a13b23fb389e35","priority":0.2475,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An executor sets require_environment but not opcert_enforce_since and is unsure whether enforcement activates"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add one sentence to Design item 1, e.g. 'Enforcement activates only when `verify.require_environment` is set AND the cert timestamp is at/after `opcert_enforce_since`; either unset = advisory.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] For the pinned_environment branch under enforcement, either delegate to trusted_env.verify_required_environment / opcert.verify_opcert (so revocation + storage-anchor era-validity are honored) or explicitly record in the plan that the claim-gate pinned path does NOT check revocation/era and why that reduced guarantee is acceptable.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.5617,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["verify_opcert_record docstring (src/rebar/_opcert_signing.py L378-382): 'the merge-gate's era/keyring recompute is deliberately NOT reproduced here'","trusted_env.verify_required_environment (src/rebar/attest/trusted_env.py L148-190) anchors key era-validity on the storage anchor and passes the full keyring including revoked_at_log_position","Plan AC2: 'the required environment must verify against its PINNED key'"],"finding":"Introducing a 'pinned_environment' trust basis into verify_opcert_record (the same-environment claim-gate path) omits the era-validity/revocation anchoring that the existing merge-gate pinned path (trusted_env.verify_required_environment -> opcert.verify_opcert with storage_anchor_position + revoked_at_log_position) performs. Under AC2 enforcement a REVOKED pinned key would still verify here, a weaker guarantee than the existing verify-opcert surface for the same pinned key.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f42117bd4b8c1b1cf","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design -> _opcert_signing.py _opcert_trust_root (pinned_environment fallback); AC2","norm_id":"n94ffe1803cfeb621","priority":0.2383,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Operator sets verify.require_environment + opcert_enforce_since; a pinned key is later revoked in trusted_environments.yaml; a cert signed under the revoked key still passes the claim gate because this path ignores revoked_at_log_position"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7222,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Confirm no existing helper (in `rebar.attest`) or already-imported dependency (`cryptography`) can extract the embedded SSHSIG public key before hand-rolling `embedded_public_key`; if none exists, note that in the design to justify the new binary parser.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'add `embedded_public_key(signature)`: parse the armored SSHSIG blob (`MAGIC || version || publickey || namespace || reserved || hash_alg || signature`)'","src/rebar/attest/sshsig.py interacts with SSHSIG only via `ssh-keygen -Y` subprocess; no existing blob-parsing helper (search for 'embedded_public_key' returned no matches)","resolve_symbol: `cryptography` EXISTS in the installed environment (may already provide SSH public-key parsing); an `sshsig` PyPI package also exists (UNRESOLVED here is not proof of absence)"],"finding":"`embedded_public_key(signature)` hand-rolls a binary parser for the armored SSHSIG blob (MAGIC || version || publickey || namespace || reserved || hash_alg || signature). The repo currently interacts with SSHSIG exclusively via the `ssh-keygen` subprocess (src/rebar/attest/sshsig.py) and has no existing blob parser; meanwhile `cryptography` is installed in the environment and may already expose SSH public-key extraction. The plan should confirm no existing helper (in `rebar.attest` or an already-imported dependency) can extract the embedded key before adding a new hand-written binary parser, since a manual SSHSIG-format parser is new maintenance/attack surface.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f64a5e46a0c027022","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design → `src/rebar/attest/sshsig.py` — add `embedded_public_key(signature)`","norm_id":"n2eafb43ec7652e77","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Extracting the signer's own public half to feed the `-Y verify` path for an unpinned but self-consistent envelope (trust_basis: envelope_key)"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"na","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reword the envelope_key basis so it does not claim the principal binding is 'checked in full' — state that under trust_basis:'envelope_key' the signature is verified against a self-supplied key and the principal is self-referential (not anchored to a known environment), matching the honest framing already in the 'unobtainable-signer-key decision' section.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6763,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'the key is fed to the normal -Y verify path, so the signature, the namespace, and the principal binding are all still checked in full'","Plan already concedes the weaker basis: 'just not tied to a KNOWN environment ... trust_basis: \"envelope_key\"'","SshsigScheme.verify (src/rebar/attest/sshsig.py L134-159) builds allowed_signers from trust_root + uses signatures[0].keyid as -I principal; when trust_root is the envelope's own key both operands are certificate-supplied"],"finding":"The design's claim that feeding the envelope-embedded key to `-Y verify` means 'the principal binding [is] still checked in full' overstates the guarantee: the allowed_signers line is built by rebar from the record's OWN claimed principal + the envelope's OWN embedded key, so both sides of the binding come from the same untrusted certificate. Verification proves the blob is internally self-consistent (signature matches its embedded key), not that the principal is anchored to any external identity — trust-equivalent to check-novalidate despite mechanically using -Y verify.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f11ee0c9c21b0ca9e","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design -> sshsig.py embedded_public_key; 'The unobtainable-signer-key decision, made explicitly'","norm_id":"nee527b78d3837861","priority":0.1237,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer reads 'principal binding checked in full' and assumes envelope_key basis defends against a mis-attributed principal, when it only defends against blob corruption"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation"